auses are stress, poor water quality, a recent move or shipping, illness, or breeding. Test the water, fix any problems and give the fish a few stable weeks; in most cases the kok recovers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can food make a flowerhorn’s kok bigger?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A quality pellet helps a fish reach its genetic potential, but no food adds kok the fish was not going to grow. Overfeeding rich foods to push the head often causes bloat and poor water, which can shrink it."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do mirrors help a flowerhorn grow a kok?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A mirror makes a flowerhorn flare and look bigger for a short time, but there is no good evidence it builds lasting kok size. Overuse causes stress, so keep any sessions brief and never leave a mirror in the tank."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between a water kok and a hard kok?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A water kok is large, soft and round, while a hard kok is smaller and firmer. They are hobby terms rather than scientific ones, and sellers use them loosely."}}]}]}</script>
