horn?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "There isn’t a single two-fish recipe. The red devil and trimac are the parents named most often, but blood parrots, Midas cichlids, festae and later Vieja cichlids were all used, and different strains carry different mixes."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why are flowerhorns illegal in some places?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Because released flowerhorns have become invasive in parts of Southeast Asia. Australia bans their import. In the United States they are legal to keep in most places, but check your state and local rules, and never release one."}}]}]}</script>
